cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "label-vs-evidence: profile anchoring in pedagogy-aware LLM judges"
message: >-
  If you use this repository — the code, the frozen study materials, or the
  released results — please cite the paper below.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bydeng01/ability-levels-audit"
abstract: >-
  Pre-registered audit of whether a pedagogy-aware LLM judge grounds its rating
  in a learner's demonstrated competence or anchors on the learner profile it is
  shown. Ships the frozen stimuli, labels, judge instrument, per-rep provenance
  and the registered analysis for the 990-call study.
keywords:
  - LLM-as-a-judge
  - automated evaluation
  - pre-registration
  - intelligent tutoring systems
  - censored rating scales
